<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1. </span><span id="S4.T1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Legend of variable names of the network given by Fig. 2B in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite> (with 7 red output nodes omitted).</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.Thmexample3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmexample3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 4.3</span></span><span id="S4.Thmexample3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmexample3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmexample3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmexample3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The base ring is <math id="S4.Thmexample3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}_{9}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mn>9</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}_{9}</annotation></semantics></math> and the state space is <math id="S4.Thmexample3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}_{9}^{22}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ℤ</mi><mn>9</mn><mn>22</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}_{9}^{22}</annotation></semantics></math>. The update functions of the nodes are provided in Table 2.</span></p>
</div>
